            "content": "# The Nix dev shell (flake.nix) and CI install the toolchain from two different\n# pins: CI reads .node-version and package.json's packageManager, while the\n# dev shell takes whatever nixpkgs packages as nodejs_22 and pnpm_12 at the\n# flake.lock revision. Nothing else notices when the two drift apart, and a\n# drifted pnpm fails or silently runs as another version\n# (docs/development/runtime-and-package-manager.md). This workflow builds the\n# dev shell and fails when its toolchain disagrees with the repository pins.\n#\n# Path-filtered, so it runs only when a pin can move. A path-filtered workflow\n# cannot be a required check: on an unrelated pull request it never reports\n# and the requirement stays pending.\n#\n# Actions are pinned to commit SHAs (comment = the release tag they resolve to).\n\nname: Dev shell\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    paths:\n      - flake.nix\n      - flake.lock\n      - .envrc\n      - .node-version\n      - package.json\n      - .github/workflows/dev-shell.yml\n  push:\n    branches: [master]\n    paths:\n      - flake.nix\n      - flake.lock\n      - .envrc\n      - .node-version\n      - package.json\n      - .github/workflows/dev-shell.yml\n\n# Pull request runs supersede each other; each master run has its own group,\n# so none is cancelled or replaced while pending.\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.ref || github.run_id }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  toolchain:\n    name: Toolchain agreement\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@9c091bb21b7c1c1d1991bb908d89e4e9dddfe3e0 # v7.0.0\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      # No Nix store cache: the shell is two packages from cache.nixos.org.\n      - uses: cachix/install-nix-action@448cde739abec1eaf0646249e3d25bb8d9bc7702 # v31.11.2\n\n      # Evaluates every flake output on ev